WEBVTT

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.860
Honestly, what a foolish,
childish thing to do.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.360
Playing with toys before an

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.910
important fight could get someone hurt.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.200
It was the best way to implement
the plan with zero waste.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.020
Still, it wouldn't have been all bad

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.760
if you had just beaten him
and forced him to obey.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.120
What we must do is to play the Game

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.210
with Kaito Daimon and the others.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.460
Attempting to scout Galileo was
a waste, nothing more.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.190
Where's the harm?

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.370
There was no change to the Game.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.970
Isn't that right, Whist?

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.870
Indeed, sir.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.230
"You shall allow me to enjoy the game
that is about to begin."

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.480
Such is the word of Klondike.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.980
Oh, Klondike said that?

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.240
We shall have a game, eh?

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.710
Then our fight must not
be an unseemly one.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.710
Well, shall we go?

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:13.400
Let's play up.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.940
Lost

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.070
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.990
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.870
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.250
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.960
Found

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.170
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:55.670
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.470
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:01.600
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.930
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.810
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.520
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.900
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.110
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.480
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.950
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.660
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.490
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:25.330
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.500
It's now or never

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.580
That is what they say

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.670
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:34.340
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.500
That is what they say

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.670
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:41.180
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.390
That is what they say

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.810
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.020
The Battle is Investigating the Puzzle

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.460
File No. 29:

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:58.030
Speculation Regarding the Orpheus Order.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.450
Judging from our encounters,

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.520
I had concluded they act in
tandem, as a group of five.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.720
But considering that Gammon was

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.720
approached individually this last time,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.210
they may not be as
uniform as we'd thought.

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:14.370
Going forward, I will make collecting
individual data a priority

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.280
and continue to gather information.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.380
That is all.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.360
Say, Ana, don't you think
this place is nice?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.700
The Pride of England
This Luxury, Large-scale Shopping Mall
is Now Open!

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.220
The popular, talked-about
spot Prouder Horse!

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.580
It's a giant shopping mall from England!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.780
English sweets!

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.460
Tea!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.210
Tea sets!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.260
I want them all!

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.300
Then why didn't you buy them?

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.470
When we were in England?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.050
We were running around the place;
no time for shopping.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.390
Come on, let's go, Ana!

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.720
Prouder Horse?

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.970
Just a mini vegetable sandwich?

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:21.320
Dude, is that enough for you?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.720
Not to worry.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.360
It has more than enough nutrients.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.370
Hey, Q-taro, you won't be able
to fight if you're hungry.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.530
"Q-taro"?

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.290
In any case, I'm busy.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.920
I, Ana, think you won't get bigger
if you don't eat more, Q-taro.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.200
Sir! I'll take a curry,
fried rice and a milk too!

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.940
Now that's what makes a boy!

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.140
You're a boy too, aren't you?

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.890
Hey there, everyone!
We brought some tea.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:06.960
Tea!

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.410
Thank you.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.680
You all right, Cube?

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.890
Why not have some tea?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:12.930
I ate too much.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.430
I couldn't have a single drop.

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:17.330
That was tryin' too much too soon.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.410
Nope, if he keeps at it,

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.960
he'll even surpass you, Gammon.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.930
What's with this cup?

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.090
It's a puzzle?

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.090
Yes! I, Ana, made it!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.040
You did a great job with this.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.420
I worked hard at it.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.100
Ow, it's hot!

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:40.540
It's so hot, I can't
solve the puzzle! Ow!

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.110
Drink it all first!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.200
Ow! Ow!

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.540
We've found you.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.670
You all!

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:00.620
Why are you here?!

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.380
The Orpheus Order!

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.510
Kaito, those school uniforms...

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:11.180
Yeah, they're from the
Crossfield Academy.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.920
That's right, Kaito.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:17.950
We're from the Crossfield Academy.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.950
The very place of learning
you previously attended.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.190
What do you mean?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.440
Even seeing us like this,
he still doesn't remember.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:29.780
How rude.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:31.870
"Remember"?

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:33.880
Well?

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:37.820
What business do you Crossfield Academy
students have here?

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:41.040
I haven't heard anything about
a mutual exchange program.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.410
Would you mind going elsewhere?

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.840
We have business with
the Phi-Brain children.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:56.950
Kaito Daimon, Gammon Sakanoue,
Cubik Galois, Ana Gram...

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.810
You veteran Phi-Brain children...

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:04.320
We of the Orpheus Order make
this formal declaration.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.510
A declaration of war!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.360
War?

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:15.290
We even wore formal clothing here

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:18.290
to more properly invite
you to our castle.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.160
There you have it.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.290
Feelin' a bit desperate
since I found your hideout?

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.380
We will attempt to neither run nor hide.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:30.380
You will of course accept
our challenge, yes?

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.070
Screw you!

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.140
You've done whatever
the hell you've wanted.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:37.180
What's so "formal" about it now?!

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:41.360
I'll make you a promise that if

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.270
you all win, you'll never see us again.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.890
But if we win,

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:52.980
you will devote yourself to
the plans of the Orpheus Order.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.580
For life.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.820
Are you an idiot?!

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:57.920
There's no way we'd buy that-

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.960
We accept your challenge!

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.120
We'll crush you all!

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.490
That way, you'll never pull
this stupid crap again.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.360
Wait, Gammon-

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.310
He's right.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:12.380
If we do that, they'll have
nothing more to do with Kaito.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.640
I, Ana, agree.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.840
You killed my cup!

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.940
Where do you all get
off just sayin' "Yes"?

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.900
You have a reason to refuse?

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:23.990
Nope.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.740
Fine, I'll go too!

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:30.460
We have not invited you.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:31.970
Otherwise, it's five against four!

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:32.990
That's not fair!

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.490
I won't hear any more complaints!

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.990
I guess it can't be helped.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.690
Hey, hang on!

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.070
The other person would be
Upperclassman Jikukawa, right?!

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.000
No, I'd like to ask him to stay behind.

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.850
Cubik, are you for real?!

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.540
Upperclassman Jikukawa,
we can count on you, right?

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.820
Understood.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.880
I'll be awaiting your return in the lab.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:08:59.560
Sir, you ain't comin'?!

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:02.850
I wasn't named in this.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:05.310
Nonoha, watch the others for me.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.310
S..Sir!

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.370
Whoa, what is this?!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.680
We're like celebs! It's like a dream!

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.320
Ana, look!

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.230
Uh, honestly! Where
do those Orpheus Order

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:40.100
people think they're taking us?

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.100
We shall soon be arriving.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:44.790
Where, where?

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.070
I can't see it.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.820
Look! Prouder Horse!

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.490
Wait, what? That's where we're going?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.030
No way! For real?!

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:03.790
Ah...

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.300
I wonder what they could be planning,

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.450
taking us to a place like that?

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.590
I thought as much.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:13.710
It's a simple puzzle.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:16.350
Rearrange the letters in
"Prouder Horse" and...

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:21.260
Now it's Orpheus Order!

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:26.020
Meaning that is their "castle," huh?

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.880
It's so gorgeous!

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:46.290
And huge!

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.400
Wow...

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.040
Nice...

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:53.040
Cute...

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.550
Look delicious...

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.140
I never thought this
is how I'd come here.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:01.390
You can go explore on your own.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.940
I couldn't do that, could I?!

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.440
We shall soon be arriving
at the puzzle floor.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.380
This way.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:20.910
Wh..What is this?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.910
A skating rink?

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.790
This shall be the stage for the battle:

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.970
a competition-style puzzle rink slider.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:31.870
Rink slider...

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:41.380
There are twelve sliders atop the rink.

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:44.440
Players ride the sliders and compete,

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.830
aiming for the goal in the center.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:51.440
Wait! We're really high.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.410
Players can move to connecting sliders

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:56.640
either vertically or horizontally.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.630
The slider they board can be moved in a

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.310
straight line vertically or horizontally,

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:05.280
and won't stop until it hits
the wall or another slider.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.850
Opponents will take turns repeating this,

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:13.270
with the winner being whoever
reaches the center goal.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.870
In no way may players
receive outside advice.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:21.350
We shall hold five games,

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.870
the winner being
the first team to win three times.

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:24.970
No objections?

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:29.450
Very well, I shall now
assign your opponent cards.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:30.810
Hold it!

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.770
You don't gotta do that.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.190
I'm gonna fight Doubt!

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:36.840
That's right.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:39.530
She got me last time too.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.400
Oh, my, is that so?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.530
Huh? Did I lose?

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:46.410
Yes, you did.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:49.670
Now, now, we can't have you just
making your own decisions.

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.560
Where's the harm?

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.420
Why not fight again using
the same opponent cards?

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:57.210
I don't mind.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.710
Well, I guess it's all right.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.210
Very well.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.560
Now to assign the order of the matches...

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:14.660
The first game is Mr. Cubik Galois
and Miss Melancholy.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:20.070
Second game: Mr. Kaito
Daimon and Mr. Pinochle.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:25.070
Third game: Mr. Ana
Gram and Mrs. Mizerka.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:30.580
Fourth game: Mr. Gammon
Sakanoue and Mr. Doubt.

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.450
Last game: Mr. Freecell and-

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.180
I..I'm his opponent?!

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:38.080
Of course you ain't!

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:40.540
Then, Kaito, you can go again.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.050
Okay.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.590
Now then, I ask that you get ready.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.600
Cube, do your best!

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.770
I'm glad it's someone
I've fought once before.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.460
That will make this easier.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.660
There are too many things we don't know

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:12.100
about the Orpheus Order.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:14.520
Where those Rings came from, for example.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:15.450
True enough.

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:18.770
In any case, I want more data on them.

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:24.270
Once I capture their data,

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:26.550
we'll get our revenge with these puzzles!

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.040
They can't transmit!

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.780
Huh? What's this?

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:38.560
Cube's bug mecha?

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:43.880
Allow me to make one announcement:

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:48.280
This floor is installed with
electronic jamming devices.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.280
Any electrical-based espionage
will not be possible.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.390
Mr. Cubik shall go first.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.800
Are both of you ready?

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.400
Ready any time.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.680
I'm prepared.

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:12.120
Very well, first game...

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.300
Play.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.070
A rink slider...

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:19.390
It's simple, but requires
a high level of strategy.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.010
The key is to read the opponent's

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:24.750
movements and add them to your own.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.240
That's a strange vehicle
you're riding, isn't it?

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:47.780
It's not a vehicle.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:49.420
He's my friend.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.600
If I use ultrasonic control mode...

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:05.660
You seem extremely hesitant.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.510
Does your tummy hurt?

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:08.960
You shut up!

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.880
Well, I'm just worried.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:13.070
Your worrying doesn't make me happier.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.370
Going that way, are you?

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.120
Then, so will I.

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:22.700
Well, where shall you go next?

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:25.970
We've met again, haven't we?

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.840
Why do you keep following me?

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:35.020
Oh, my, why do you run?

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.870
Are you blushing, perhaps?

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.140
How cute.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:46.820
It's not as if I hate you, you know.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.820
Huh?!

00:16:56.650 --> 00:16:58.450
After all, I understand.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:03.120
You want revenge on me,
for giving you the pain of defeat.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.440
That feeling...

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.180
It's the same as me.

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:19.970
I fight for revenge too!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:25.440
Yes, for revenge against Kaito Daimon!

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.310
What?

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:28.560
Against me?

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.770
That man toyed with me, betrayed me,

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:35.650
left my heart and body in tatters.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:38.880
Kaito, for real?!

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:40.030
It's news to me!

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:45.660
This is what that man once said
about a puzzle I'd made:

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:48.170
"Uh, it's so-so."

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.540
He said that!

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:50.960
Huh?

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:55.690
To me, who was raised as
a flower, as a butterfly.

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:58.160
What's more, he doesn't remember!

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.230
That's far too cruel, isn't it?

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.270
But with this...

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.370
I could beat Kaito Daimon,

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:09.020
put him on the ground
groveling for forgiveness.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:11.280
Most unsightly.

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:15.990
That eye!

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.780
The Orpheus Ring is active.

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:30.290
You're not going to chase me anymore?

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.750
If you weren't Kaito Daimon's friends,

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.000
we may have really gotten along.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:37.550
Too bad.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.350
I don't think so!

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:42.550
He did it! Cube is in reach!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.200
Not good, huh?

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.160
Yeah.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.440
That wasn't nice.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.780
I thought she'd come after me.

00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:59.290
My calculations are all off now!

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:05.770
True enough, her thought
speed is increasing.

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:10.220
Melancholy, be careful!

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:12.000
He's hiding something.

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:17.510
Can you not tell this is a pivotal
moment right now, O Sister?!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.970
My victory is assured.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.030
Yet still you would continue?

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:27.440
Of course!

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.520
How could I quit at a time like this?!

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:32.240
There are still things I can do!

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:38.360
It's no good; there's
nothing more you can do.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.620
With this, victory is mine.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.890
Now then, my apologies.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.730
First game, winner: Miss Melancholy.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:24.410
I did it!

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:28.290
Sister, I won!

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:31.000
You did well, Melancholy.

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:34.010
Cube...

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.340
I lost.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:42.480
Cube, cheer up.

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:45.010
But I got what I needed.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.330
During the puzzle,

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:49.260
I had my bug mecha
capture Melancholy's data.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.250
But weren't you unable to

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.270
use the bug mecha because
of electrical jamming?

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:58.060
I thought this might happen,

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:00.780
so I used the ultrasonic control
mode that I'd installed.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:06.270
Still, it was tough because I had to
keep manually controlling it.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:18.730
Yes, that's right.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:22.420
Please analyze the data
that I'm about to send you.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.150
Yes...

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:29.100
Thank you, Manager Maze.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.980
That was good work, Edison.

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:36.780
Huh?! So...

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:40.920
You solved the puzzle while
controlling the bug mecha?

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:41.960
The whole time?

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:44.950
Yes, but losing is losing.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:50.490
Don't worry about it, Cubik.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:53.450
We can turn one loss around soon enough.

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:55.210
Yes!

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.570
Everyone...

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:12.100
Kaito, I will have you make good.

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:17.920
By this pendant, the
promise you made to me.

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:21.980
Promise?

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.330
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:45.210
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:51.640
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:54.430
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:59.520
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:07.950
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:13.490
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:17.330
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.920
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:24.960
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.670
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:31.050
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:34.720
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:38.730
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:43.020
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:46.360
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:51.660
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:53.070
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.540
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:05.170
You've lost, Kaito Daimon.

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:07.160
I know everything about you.

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:09.800
Hold on! What do you know about Kaito?

00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:11.630
Did you know when I put on my sunglasses,

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:13.150
I know the strength of my opponent?

00:24:13.150 --> 00:24:14.890
Did you know they shoot beams?

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:17.610
Did you know that these are
transforming eyeglasses?!

00:24:17.610 --> 00:24:20.000
Wait, "eyeglasses" isn't
a good way to put it.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:21.960
Yes, they're Self-contained,
All-purpose Aid-

00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:26.670
The Promise

00:24:21.960 --> 00:24:23.620
Next time, "The Promise"

00:24:23.620 --> 00:24:26.360
All right, Pinochle,
let's trade information!
